Constrained MPC with one controller per node of a `velocities × altitudes` grid of flight
conditions, solving only the nodes of the grid cell the aircraft is in.

`wv` and `wh` are the hat-function weights of two `LinearMPCScheduler`s, one weight per knot
of each axis, so node `(i, j)` has the bilinear weight `wv[i] * wh[j]`, positive for at
most the four corners of the current cell. Every tick those nodes solve their QPs for the
same state, reference and previous command, and `u` is the weighted blend of their first
moves, as in `LinearMPCScheduledOptimizer`.

The controllers live in `EnvelopeMPC.grid_bank`, which builds a node
(`VelocityMPC.member_controller`) the first time it gets a positive weight. The component's
size grows with the knots of each axis, not with their product, and a grid of any size
costs nothing until it is flown through; `built` counts the nodes built so far. The QPs are
solved by LinearMPC.jl's Julia solver, so a model containing this component does not export
